lesson: 160
title: Olympiad: how many digits number the pages of a book
level: primary-3
stars: 3
explain: Pages 1 to 9 use one digit each: 9 digits. Pages 10 to 99 are 90 pages with two digits each: 180 digits. Up to page 99 that is 189 digits.
explain: Every page from 100 on uses three digits. So take away 189, divide by 3, and add the result to 99.
explain: A book numbered with 270 digits: 270 - 189 = 81, 81 ÷ 3 = 27 pages after page 99, so the book has 99 + 27 = 126 pages.
vars: a=name n=100..500
let: D = 3 * n - 108
answer: n
exercise: To number the pages of a book from 1 onwards, a printer used {D} digits in all. How many pages does the book have?
exercise: {a} numbered every page of a notebook, starting at 1, and wrote {D} digits altogether. How many pages does the notebook have?
exercise: The pages of a book are numbered 1, 2, 3 and so on. Printing all the page numbers takes {D} digits. How many pages are there?
exercise: The page numbers of a book use {D} digits altogether, and the first page is page 1. How many pages does the book have?
test: How many pages are in a book whose page numbers, starting from 1, are made of {D} digits in all?
test: {a} typed the whole numbers from 1 upwards, one after another, and pressed digit keys {D} times. Which number did {a.he} type last?
test: Every seat in a big hall gets a number: 1, 2, 3 and so on. The painter painted {D} digits. How many seats are in the hall?
exercise: A printer in Boston used {D} digits to print the page numbers of a book, starting with page 1. How many pages does the book have?
exercise: How many pages does a book have if its page numbers, beginning at 1, need {D} digits altogether?
exercise: {a} wrote the number of every page in {a.his} diary, from page 1 to the last page. That took {D} digits in total. How many pages are in the diary?
exercise: Numbering a photo album from page one to the end uses {D} digits combined. How many pages does the album have?
exercise: {D} digits were needed to number every page of a school atlas in London, starting at 1. How many pages has the atlas got?
exercise: A book's pages go 1, 2, 3 and so on up to the last page, and all those page numbers together are made of {D} digits. What is the number of the last page?
exercise: {a} stamped page numbers in a scrapbook, one page after another from 1, and stamped {D} digits in all. How many pages did {a.he} number?
exercise: The page numbers from 1 to the end of a novel use {D} digits. Find how many pages the novel has.
test: {a} in Melbourne counted every digit in the page numbers of a storybook that starts at page 1, and got {D}. How many pages does the storybook have?
test: The houses on a long street in Ottawa are numbered 1, 2, 3 and so on, one number for each house. The numbers on all the doors use {D} digits. How many houses are on the street?
test: A sign maker in Cork cut out metal digits for the numbers of the lockers in a gym, from locker 1 to the last locker. He cut {D} digits. How many lockers are there?
test: Find the last page of a book whose page numbering, from 1, uses {D} digits altogether.
test: Raffle tickets are numbered from 1 upwards with no gaps, and printing all the numbers took {D} digits. How many tickets were printed?
test: Writing out all the whole numbers from 1 up to some number takes {D} digits. Which number is the last one written?
exercise: printer used {D} digits for the page numbers, starts at page 1. how many pages that book got
exercise: numbered me notebook pages from 1, wrote {D+3} digits — no wait, {D} digits. how many pages
exercise: {a} says {D} digits ÷ 3 = {D/3} pages. nah that's wrong, the small pages got less digits. how many pages really
exercise: page numbers from 1 up, {D} digits all together, oh and the book cost 12 dollar. how many pages
test: lockers numbered 1 2 3 n so on, the guy painted {D} digits. how many lockers we got
test: typed numbers 1 upwards, hit the digit keys {D+2} times, sorry, {D} times. last number i typed?
test: diary pages numbered from page 1, {D} digits used, it's got a red cover lol. what's the last page number
exam: It is given that, for the numbering of the pages of a book commencing at 1, a total of {D} digits were employed. Determine the number of pages of which the book consists.
exam: Whereas {a} numbered consecutively every page of a notebook, commencing with the number 1, and wrote {D} digits in aggregate, ascertain the number of pages in the notebook.
exam: Ascertain the greatest number written when the whole numbers from 1 onwards are written in succession, the total quantity of digits employed being {D}.
exam: A printer is engaged to number the pages of a report consecutively from page 1 and employs {D} digits in so doing. State the number of pages contained in the report.
exercise: Grandad's memoirs were printed after he passed away. The printer used {D} digits to number the pages from 1. How many pages does the book have?
exercise: {a} was economical with the truth: {a.he} said {a.his} diary has "about a hundred pages". Numbering them from 1 took {D} digits. How many pages does it really have?
test: the bloody printer's "glitch" ate the page count. all we know: {D} digits numbering from 1. how many pages, then?
